L["Abby Lewis stood alone at Glenbrook Homestead, singing softly to herself. The houses were abandoned. The village was silent. She said she just wanted friends for a tea party — three stuffed animals: Mr. Munchykins, Trunksy, and Mayor Striggs. You found them, each one near a place where something had clearly gone very wrong. Abby appeared each time to recite a cheerful little rhyme. The rhymes were about the dead."] = "Abby Lewis stood alone at Glenbrook Homestead, singing softly to herself. The houses were abandoned. The village was silent. She said she just wanted friends for a tea party — three stuffed animals: Mr. Munchykins, Trunksy, and Mayor Striggs. You found them, each one near a place where something had clearly gone very wrong. Abby appeared each time to recite a cheerful little rhyme. The rhymes were about the dead."
L["Above the ice, at the roof of the world, the Frozen Throne waits. The Ashen Verdict — Argent Crusade and Ebon Blade, bound by a single purpose — stands at the citadel's door. Highlord Tirion Fordring lifts the Ashbringer. Every victory in Northrend, every fallen soldier, every mile of ground bought in blood has led here. One way or another, the reign of Arthas Menethil ends at the summit."] = "Above the ice, at the roof of the world, the Frozen Throne waits. The Ashen Verdict — Argent Crusade and Ebon Blade, bound by a single purpose — stands at the citadel's door. Highlord Tirion Fordring lifts the Ashbringer. Every victory in Northrend, every fallen soldier, every mile of ground bought in blood has led here. One way or another, the reign of Arthas Menethil ends at the summit."
