L["Calydus pointed you toward Ulthalesh — the Deadwind Harvester, a scythe of terrible power that had reaped souls for millennia. You followed the curse through Deadwind Pass, where the Dark Riders still haunted the roads. In their shadowed lair, you tore Ulthalesh from their grasp. The scythe's whispers joined the chorus in your mind — a weapon that was never truly silent."] = "Calydus pointed you toward Ulthalesh — the Deadwind Harvester, a scythe of terrible power that had reaped souls for millennia. You followed the curse through Deadwind Pass, where the Dark Riders still haunted the roads. In their shadowed lair, you tore Ulthalesh from their grasp. The scythe's whispers joined the chorus in your mind — a weapon that was never truly silent."
L["Calydus revealed the location of the Scepter of Sargeras — a weapon capable of tearing holes between dimensions, wielded by the Dark Titan's own lieutenants. You found it sealed in a vault warded against mortal hands. But a warlock's hands were never quite mortal. You broke the wards, claimed the Scepter, and felt the fabric of reality shudder around you. The power to break worlds was now in your grip."] = "Calydus revealed the location of the Scepter of Sargeras — a weapon capable of tearing holes between dimensions, wielded by the Dark Titan's own lieutenants. You found it sealed in a vault warded against mortal hands. But a warlock's hands were never quite mortal. You broke the wards, claimed the Scepter, and felt the fabric of reality shudder around you. The power to break worlds was now in your grip."
L["Calydus spoke of the Skull of the Man'ari — an eredar artifact of staggering summoning power. The ritual reagents alone were dangerous enough to kill a lesser warlock. You gathered them, performed the summoning, and wrested the Skull from the eredar lord who guarded it. The Skull's eyes glowed with malevolent intelligence, as if the demon trapped within was already planning its next move."] = "Calydus spoke of the Skull of the Man'ari — an eredar artifact of staggering summoning power. The ritual reagents alone were dangerous enough to kill a lesser warlock. You gathered them, performed the summoning, and wrested the Skull from the eredar lord who guarded it. The Skull's eyes glowed with malevolent intelligence, as if the demon trapped within was already planning its next move."
